  "id": "directed-forgetting",
  "term": "directed forgetting",
  "definition": "Directed forgetting is the intentional effort to reduce later remembering of particular information. It is an active form of forgetting used to keep no-longer-relevant or outdated material from interfering with current thinking and recall.",
